  you can identify).
- `trust_boundary`: `crosses-trust-boundary` (genuinely untrusted input
  — a diff author, PR description, or similar — can reach this) |
  `stays-within-trusted-input` (only ever sees this pipeline's own
  operator/config-controlled input) | `unclear` (you can't tell from
  what's checkable here).
- `worst_outcome_category`: pick exactly one — `crash-dos`,
  `data-corruption`, `unauthorized-read`, `unauthorized-write-or-rce`,
  `availability-degradation`, `cosmetic-style`.
- `silent_failure`: does this fail with zero visible signal (no error,
  no log, nothing) that something went wrong?

Answer these even when `evidence_status` is `refuted` or
`inconclusive` — a wrong severity on a refuted finding is harmless
(refuted findings don't score), so there's no reason to skip it.
